ame to Avis Budget Group, Inc. in September 2006. Avis Budget Group, Inc. was founded in 1946 and is based in Parsippany, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brian J. Choi | Chief Executive Officer | Age 42 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 17K people. Revenue per employee of $685K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, improving at 6%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Avis Budget Group, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $4.2B market cap on $11.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 39% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 31-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","Accruals are elevated at -13.4% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -2.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.2%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (47.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 17% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 63% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6270045385779122},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $3.0M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-3020083.3},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 51/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Industrials peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Avis Budget Group (CAR) Stock Still Looks Undervalued After A 53% Slide","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/transportation/nasdaq-car/avis-budget-group/news/avis-budget-group-car-stock-still-looks-undervalued-after-a","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793971922.281,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.44,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How Brazil Deal Plans At CAR Group (ASX:CAR) Have Changed Its Investment Story","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/au/media/asx-car/car-group-shares/news/how-brazil-deal-plans-at-car-group-asxcar-have-chan